1auk|n|A diamond-shaped figure usually with the upper and lower angles slightly acute, borne upon a shield or escutcheon. Cf. Fusil. ; A form of the escutcheon used by women instead of the shield which is used by men. ; A figure with four equal sides, having two acute and two obtuse angles; a rhomb. ; Anything in the form of lozenge. ; A small cake of sugar and starch, flavored, and often medicated. -- originally in the form of a lozenge.	a:8o9,113,3~8o9,113,3
